      {
        "Id": "3a2d8512557641f2b106cb6e484d727f",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE:  type a colour for each part:  a name (NAVY, BLUEPRINT, DARKGREY, TEAL, PURPLE, MAROON, OLIVE, GREEN, BLACK, WHITE, CREAM, LIGHTGREY), or R,G,B (e.g. 40,50,70), or #RRGGBB.  RESET = back to normal, blank = keep.  0 = ribbon, 1 = Properties, 2 = Project Browser (title bar + frame; the list inside is drawn by Revit), 3 = drawing area background.  Dark colours give white text, light colours dark text.  RUN False = preview, True = change.  Kept after a Revit restart.",
